"Somali, Eritrean and Sudanese kitchens do not exist as standalone restaurants in the Triangle - the searches return only Ethiopian houses, one of which markets itself as Ethiopian and Eritrean but cooks an injera-and-wot menu indistinguishable from the two already scored. The same is true of Ghanaian, Georgian, Armenian and Israeli cooking: no restaurant in the named towns, and the nearest Georgian option sits outside the area entirely. Taiwanese kitchens do exist here, but none of them carries a dish that clears the bar this document sets for a complete meal."
